BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Idomeneo by Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261114
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261115
UID:007852f5fcee85d7c1e2517b3b18cb77@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:LOVE VS. DUTY\nAfter King Idomeneo returns to Crete from the T
 rojan War\, the high-stakes consequences of a desperate deal he struck wit
 h Neptune for safe passage reveal themselves when he must choose between h
 is own son\, Idamante\, and the vow he made to the sea god\, further compl
 icated as Idamante is loved by both the Trojan princess Ilia and the jealo
 us Greek princess Elettra. But when divine wrath is incurred\, Idamante an
 d Ilia prove their worth\, prompting Neptune’s mercy.\nBased on a 1705 p
 lay by Crébillion père\, Mozart’s first mature opera demonstrates his 
 mastery of orchestration\, accompanied recitatives\, and lyrical beauty. W
 hile it premiered in 1781 in Munich\, it did not see its U.S. premiere unt
 il 1947\, at Tanglewood.\nArtistic Staff\nConductor\nArthur Fagen\nStage D
 irector\nRobin Guarino\nSet Designer\nAndrew Boyce\nCostume Designer\nJess
 ica Pabst\nLighting Designer\nThomas Hase\nVideo Designer\nNicholas Husson
 g\nWig & Makeup Designer\nAndrew Elliot\nChorus Master\nLisa Hasson\nDicti
 on Coach\nStefano de Peppo\nSupertitle Author\nCori Ellison
GEO:39.1665575;-86.51751229999999
LOCATION:Musical Arts Center\, 101 N Eagleson Ave\, Bloomington\, IN 47406
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/idomeneo-by-wolfgang-amadeus-mo
 zart/59736/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
