BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mainstage in Concert &#8211\; Symphony No. 3\, Circus Maximus by J
 ohn Corigliano
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261117T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261117T203000
UID:db63d8cf711dbc6f7dee67705c93f771@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:John Corigliano’s massive 2005 work for a large concert band
  is known for its intensity and theatricality as it stretches the boundari
 es of the wind ensemble. A synthesis of genres\, the piece references jazz
 \, martial fanfares\, circus music\, and hunting calls\, interspersed with
  lyrical passages. Interested in immersing the audience\, both spatially a
 nd metaphorically\, Corigliano employs an onstage ensemble\, a marching ba
 nd\, and a 12-gauge shotgun\, and places the audience as if they were at t
 he center of an arena\, such as ancient Rome’s Circus Maximus.\nIn a sym
 phonic portrait of a world caught between competing realities\, Corigliano
  compares today’s ubiquitous obsession with entertainment and violence t
 o the ancient Romans enjoying the sight of lions devouring human beings fo
 r amusement\, writing that “The parallels between the high decadence of 
 Rome and our present time are obvious.” \nGeorge Gershwin’s iconic Rha
 psody in Blue will begin this must-experience evening.\nArtistic Staff\nEn
 semble\nWind Ensemble\nConductor\nDonald McKinney\nGuest Artists/Soloists
 \nTBA
GEO:39.1665575;-86.5175123
LOCATION:Musical Arts Center\, 101 N Eagleson Ave\, Bloomington\, IN 47406
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/mainstage-in-concert-8211-symph
 ony-no-3-circus-maximus-by-john-corigliano/59752/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
