BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Palestine 36 w/ filmmaker | Arthouse Now
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261117T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261117T213000
UID:71e5fd2aa97675e89604b60fed0c290f@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:In 1936\, as the British Empire tightens its grip on Palestine
 \, Yusuf is caught between his village home and his work in Jerusalem. Ami
 dst an anti-colonial revolt and a workers uprising\, all sides converge in
  a decisive moment for the entire region. Weaving together multiple plotli
 nes\, empathies\, and frames of reference\, Annemarie Jacir deftly balance
 s intimate human stories—portrayed by a stellar ensemble cast—with swe
 eping political history\, using rare archival footage to ground the narrat
 ive in historical reality. [119 min\; drama\; Arabic with English subtitle
 s and English]\nA prerecorded conversation with filmmaker Annemarie Jacir
 \, unique to IU Cinema\, will screen after the film. Jacir has written\, d
 irected\, and produced over 16 films. Her films have premiered in Cannes\,
  Berlin\, Venice\, Locarno\, Rotterdam\, and Toronto. Her second work to d
 ebut in Cannes\, Salt of This Sea\, went on to win the FIPRESCI Critics Aw
 ard\, and 14 other international awards including Best Film in Milan. With
  a commitment to mentoring\, training\, and hiring locally\, Jacir also te
 aches\, actively promoting independent cinema in the region. Founder of Ph
 ilistine Films\, she collaborates regularly as an editor\, screenwriter\, 
 and producer with fellow filmmakers.
GEO:39.168585;-86.517361
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 E. 7th Street\, Bloomington\, IN 47405
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/palestine-36-w-filmmaker-arthou
 se-now/60006/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
