UID:da5719007ec28d04315b895561b95002@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:Based on the life of writer and feminist activist Suzanne Cés
 aire\, Madeleine Hunt-Ehrlich’s debut feature explores the relationships
  with Césaire’s husband\, French politician Aimé Césaire\, and fellow
  surrealist André Breton. Shimmering with the radiance of its Caribbean l
 andscape and a phenomenal performance from Zita Hanrot\, the film breaks f
 rom traditional biographical structure\, blending more conventional narrat
 ive with captivating experimental elements. [75 min\; biography\, drama\; 
 English and French with English subtitles]
GEO:39.168585;-86.517361
