BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SNEAK PREVIEW: Ink | Additional Films and Guests
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261130T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261130T210000
UID:34589ff3bda9d3de380ed40027e79e8e@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:SNEAK PREVIEW SCREENING! See Danny Boyle's acclaimed biopic of
  media magnate Rupert Murdoch before it's available anywhere.\nIn November
  1969\, 30-something outcast British journalist Larry Lamb (Jack O’Conne
 ll—Sinners\; 28 Years Later) met a young Australian media baron named Ru
 pert Murdoch (Guy Pearce—Memento\; L.A. Confidential\; The Brutalist) an
 d a partnership began that changed the face of the news forever. In the Lo
 ndon of that era\, the media had its home on the iconic Fleet Street\, a h
 otbed of betrayal\, backstabbing\, and bad behavior\, where it was ruled b
 y the establishment. Lamb and Murdoch took a different approach\, publishi
 ng editions of The Sun loaded with lurid headlines and outlandish puns\, a
 nd covering everything from sports to television to sex\, pushing ethical 
 concerns to the sidelines\, and revolutionizing the media landscape. This 
 is the period that Academy Award-winning director Danny Boyle’s (Slumdog
  Millionaire\; 28 Days Later\; Trainspotting\; 28 Years Later) film—writ
 ten by James Graham\, whose original stage play INK won awards on both sid
 es of the Atlantic—covers\, one that saw a succession of firsts that wou
 ld alter the trajectory of today’s 24/7\, clickbait news landscape and t
 ake Lamb and Murdoch down a dark path. [116 min\; drama\; English]\nSpecia
 l thanks to our friends at Netflix for providing this advance access scree
 ning.
GEO:39.168585;-86.517361
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 E. 7th Street\, Bloomington\, IN 47405
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/sneak-preview-ink-additional-fi
 lms-and-guests/60243/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
