DESCRIPTION:At all-boys water polo camp\, a 12-year-old boy is pulled into
  a cruel tradition called The Plague\, which targets an outcast with an "i
 llness." As the lines between game and reality blur\, he fears the joke ma
 y be hiding something real. IndieWire's Critics' Pic\; Official Selection 
 of the Cannes Film Festival\; Fantastic Fest Best Picture Winner\; nominat
 ed for Best Feature\, Best Lead Performance\, and Best Breakthrough Perfor
 mance at the 2025 Independent Spirit Awards. [98 min\; drama\, thriller\; 
 English]
