BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sarah Jarosz: 10 Years of Undercurrent
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261203T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261203T223000
UID:203565bec4d1437c2b2d40128e56466c@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:Originally from Wimberley\, Texas\, Sarah Jarosz is a six-time
  GRAMMY Award winning singer\, songwriter and multi-instrumentalist. Since
  her recorded debut in 2009\, she has released seven solo albums and two a
 lbums with I’m With Her\, her band with Sara Watkins and Aoife O’Donov
 an.\nIn addition to her multiple GRAMMY\, Americana Music Association\, an
 d Folk Alliance awards\, her work has received widespread critical praise 
 from publications including Rolling Stone\, The New York Times\, and USA T
 oday. Jarosz has appeared three times on PBS’s legendary Austin City Lim
 its television show and numerous times on A Prairie Home Companion\, Live 
 From Here\, and the Grand Ole Opry. She is currently based in Nashville\, 
 Tennessee.\nJordan Tice is an award-winning guitarist and songwriter descr
 ibed by the Fretboard Journal as “quite simply\, one of our favorite aco
 ustic guitarists performing today.” He has 7 projects to his name as a s
 olo artist and 6 as a founding member of the string band\, Hawktail.\nEqua
 lly virtuosic as a flatpicker and fingerstylist\, and with a casual vocal 
 style\, Tice conjures ingredients from far-flung worlds with ease. His per
 formances call upon the repertories of American and British Isles folk\, b
 luegrass\, blues and pop-oriented songs\, and though his earlier releases 
 are instrumental in focus\, he has been carefully honing his craft as a si
 nger-songwriter in his most recent work. This includes his albums Motivati
 onal Speakeasy (produced by Kenneth Pattengale of The Milk Carton Kids and
  praised by NPR Music as “a really wonderful record”)\, Wild Rose of M
 orning (a collaboration with Andrew Marlin and Christian Sedelmyer)\, and 
 Badlettsville.\nHe has performed at festivals such as the Grey Fox Bluegra
 ss Festival\, Green Mountain Bluegrass and Roots\, Red Wing Roots\, Winter
 grass Music Festival\, and the Strawberry Music Festival and opened for ar
 tists like Watchhouse\, I’m With Her\, The Milk Carton Kids\, and Madiso
 n Cunningham. In addition to his solo and collaborative work\, he has perf
 ormed and recorded as a sideman with Americana artists such as David Rawli
 ngs\, Yola\, Andrew Marlin and Aoife O’Donovan.
GEO:39.1662844;-86.5328085
LOCATION:Buskirk-Chumley Theater\, 114 E. Kirkwood Avenue\, Bloomington\, 
 IN 47408
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/sarah-jarosz-10-years-of-underc
 urrent/59509/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
