UID:063a733294a96493eb7709c9811984f4@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:As Ellettsville Main Street Inc.'s largest event of the year\,
  Santa on Sale Street returns Saturday\, Dec. 12\, bringing hundreds of fa
 milies downtown for a morning of festive activities\, family fun and commu
 nity connection. Thanks to the generosity of local businesses\, organizati
 ons and volunteers\, nearly every activity is free. \nThe celebration begi
 ns at 9 a.m.\, with Santa making his grand entrance aboard an Ellettsville
  fire truck at 9:30 a.m. Special thanks go to the town of Ellettsville and
  the Ellettsville Fire Department for coordinating an alternate route to a
 ccommodate his arrival.\nFrom 9:45 a.m. until noon\, children can visit Sa
 nta and Mrs. Claus at the Ellettsville Branch of the Monroe County Public 
 Library\, share their Christmas wishes and enjoy the much-anticipated toy 
 giveaway. Edgewood Schools and Seven Oaks Classical School will join in th
 e holiday fun\, helping make the morning extra special for families. Volun
 teers from Edgewood Schools will keep little ones entertained with activit
 ies while they eagerly await their turn to visit Santa.\nThroughout downto
 wn\, participating businesses and organizations will open their doors with
  a variety of activities and treats for the whole family.\nThe Masonic Lod
 ge and Eastern Star will serve a breakfast buffet from 8 to 11 a.m. for $1
 0 per person\, with children age 5 and younger eating free. This is the on
 ly activity with a charge\, and all proceeds benefit Eastern Star.\nThe Cr
 aft and Catalano Insurance Group will offer activities\, while Miracle on 
 46 Church will delight children with balloon animals. Thurman Body Shop wi
 ll feature its always popular 75-foot-long die-cast car racetrack\, and Kn
 itting Romance will host crafts inside their store.\nEric Bloch will bring
  science to life with fun chemistry experiments for young explorers. The G
 rinch will also make a special appearance\, courtesy of Floor Coverings In
 ternational\, adding a little mischievous fun to the morning.\nFig Tree Ma
 rket\, The Caffeinated Cook and The IN Store will also join in the festivi
 ties. Maps will be available at participating locations to help families e
 xplore all that Santa on Sale Street has to offer. For the latest event up
 dates and a glimpse of the holiday magic from years past\, visit the Santa
  on Sale Street Facebook page.
GEO:39.2318647;-86.6277506
LOCATION:Downtown Ellettsville\, Sale Street\, Ellettsville\, IN 47429
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/santa-on-sale-street/60244/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
