DESCRIPTION:In a small woodsy Oregon town\, a group of childhood friends
 —sensitive Gordie (Wil Wheaton)\, tough guy Chris (River Phoenix)\, flam
 boyant Teddy (Corey Feldman)\, and scaredy-cat Vern (Jerry O'Connell)—ar
 e in search of a missing teenager's body. Wanting to be heroes in each oth
 er's and their hometown's eyes\, they set out on an unforgettable two-day 
 trek that turns into an odyssey of self-discovery. They sneak smokes\, tel
 l tall tales\, cuss 'cause it's cool\, and band together when the going ge
 ts tough. When they encounter the town's knife-wielding hoods who are also
  after the body\, the boys discover a strength they never knew they had. F
 illed with humor and suspense and based on the novella The Body by Stephen
  King\, Stand By Me is a rare and special film about friendship and the in
 delible experiences of growing up. [89 min\; adventure\, drama\; English]
GEO:39.168585;-86.517361
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 E. 7th Street\, Bloomington\, IN 47405
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/stand-by-me-escape-the-week-meg
 a-marathon/60203/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Life of Chuck | Escape the Week Mega Marathon
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261213T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261213T180000
UID:f0b00ccad17850464d45aeef3b870eef@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:As the world unravels\, Charles “Chuck” Krantz’s life is
  recalled in three acts\, capturing joy\, loss\, and the quiet moments tha
 t make a life feel full. The Life of Chuck is a genre-defying exploration 
 of what it means to truly be alive and have your life changed—in ways bi
 g and small—through the cast of characters you assemble throughout your 
 lifetime. Tom Hiddleston anchors an extraordinary ensemble cast—includin
 g Matthew Lillard\, Chiwetel Ejiofor\, Mark Hamill\, Jacob Tremblay\, and 
 Mia Sara—in this Stephen King adaptation by Mike Flanagan that took home
  People's Choice Award honors at the Toronto International Film Festival. 
 [111 min\; drama\, fantasy\, sci-fi\; English]
GEO:39.168585;-86.517361
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 E. 7th Street\, Bloomington\, IN 47405
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/the-life-of-chuck-escape-the-we
 ek-mega-marathon/60205/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Running Man | Escape the Week Mega Marathon
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261213T194500
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261213T213000
UID:94863eb0df10d70a9e766667b24c1a35@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:After escaping from jail\, Ben Richards (Arnold Schwarzenegger
 ) tries to prove his innocence\, but his efforts are thwarted at every tur
 n by an authoritarian regime in need of a scapegoat. Richards is captured 
 along with an innocent civilian\, Amber Mendez (Maria Conchita Alonso)\, a
 nd they are forced to participate in a violent game show called The Runnin
 g Man\, hosted by the unctuous Damon Killian (Richard Dawson). The object 
 of the game for Richards and Mendez: obtain freedom by staying alive again
 st a gauntlet of skillful assassins\, each armed with unique weapons like 
 razor-sharp hockey sticks and chainsaws. With the help of some fellow "con
 testants\," Richards is able to tap into government computers and prove hi
 s innocence. A prescient story first told by King in his 1982 dystopian th
 riller novel of the same name. [101 min\; action\, sci-fi\, thriller\; Eng
 lish\, Japanese\, Italian\, and Spanish with English subtitles]
GEO:39.168585;-86.517361
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 E. 7th Street\, Bloomington\, IN 47405
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/the-running-man-escape-the-week
 -mega-marathon/60207/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Shawshank Redemption | Escape the Week Mega Marathon
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261213T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261213T160000
UID:f001c497eef7a18c1796de06ba4ac728@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:Internationally acclaimed actors Tim Robbins and Morgan Freema
 n star in a compelling drama of hope\, friendship\, and atonement behind t
 he walls of a maximum security prison in The Shawshank Redemption. Red (Fr
 eeman)\, serving a life sentence\, and Andy Dufresne (Robbins)\, a mild-ma
 nnered banker wrongly convicted of murder\, forge an unlikely bond that wi
 ll span more than 20 years. Under horrifying conditions and the ever-prese
 nt threat of violence\, two lifers reclaim their souls and find freedom wi
 thin their hearts while languishing in the U.S. carceral system. Based on 
 the novella Rita Hayworth and the Shawshank Redemption by Stephen King. [1
 42 min\; drama\; English]
GEO:39.168585;-86.517361
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 E. 7th Street\, Bloomington\, IN 47405
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/the-shawshank-redemption-escape
 -the-week-mega-marathon/60204/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
