BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:3rd Annual Bloomington Winter Blues Fest 2027
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20270206T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20270206T223000
UID:e39dd938087b86c5e61d940e7325966e@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:Whose got the Winter Blues???\nJoin us for the 3rd Annual Bloo
 mington Winter Blues Fest featuring:\nMike Milligan and Steam Shovel\nAn O
 riginal\, Powerful\, Soulful group from Kokomo\, Indiana\, United States\,
  formed in 1993\, comprised of brothers\, Mike Milligan (guitar/vocals) an
 d Shaun Milligan (bass)\, and Robert “Tiny” Cook (drums/vocals). They 
 were honored with an award for a Lifetime of Keeping the Blues alive by th
 e Fishers Blues Festival (Indy) and performed for 5000 of their biggest fa
 ns w Robert Cray Band (5th time!) And received an achievement award from t
 he Mayor Of Muncie Indiana for the 30th anniversary! They also performed a
  sold out show w BB KING on his final Indiana show\, and recently with BUD
 DY GUY (for the 4th time)\, Los Lonely Boys (2nd x)\, Jimmie Vaughan\, and
  Robert Cray (again! for the SIXTH time!). With 7 CD releases on Mojo Hut 
 Records\, 100’s of Thousands of touring miles\, and several Thousands of
  performances under their belts…. it’s always Full Steam ahead.\nMoJo 
 Gumbo\nCelebrating 16 years of making great music together from small\, in
 timate venues to major festivals. MoJo Gumbo is a band that mixes differen
 t types of music to create it’s own special sound! Featuring Steve “Sc
 rapper” Brown on guitar and lead vocals\, Jeff Farber on Bass / Vocals\,
  Tom Lindmar Drums / Vocals\, and Marty Weaver at Keyboards. MoJo Gumbo pl
 ays music from Louisiana and the Mississippi Delta\, blending New Orleans 
 Funk\, Blues\, R&B\, Jazz\, and Zydeco into a delicious musical Flavour!\n
 Paul Holdman & Rebekah Meldrum\nPaul Holdman is a guitarist\, singer\, son
 gwriter and producer who launched his professional music career in 1990 as
  a member of the blues band Bangkok Rooster. In 1993 he toured with former
  John Mellencamp guitarist Larry Crane. During that time he started a last
 ing friendship and songwriting partnership with fellow band member Jennie 
 DeVoe. Paul co-wrote and played guitar on “Miles Away“a track from Jen
 nie’s debut album that was featured in an episode of the hit television 
 series Party of Five. He also co-wrote and performed on “How I Feel “
 \, from her second album\, which earned first place in the Billboard Magaz
 ine world song contest. Around the same period Paul did a brief stint perf
 orming with singer songwriter Carrie Newcomer where he met drummer Jamey R
 eid. Their friendship would lead to a new musical venture.\nIn 2000 Paul i
 nvited Reid to join a band he was forming with Phil Pierle and Brant Millh
 olland. The group became known as the Woomblies and eventually expanded fr
 om a four piece ensemble into the 10 member Woomblies Rock Orchestra. The 
 band has released two albums of original music and continues to perform to
  enthusiastic sold out audiences throughout Indiana. Paul’s musical part
 nerships often span decades. During his early Bangkok Rooster years he met
  fellow musician Gordon Bonham\, a friendship and collaboration that has e
 ndured for more than 35 years. In 2000 Paul met acclaimed soul blues artis
 t Tad Robinson\, an 11 time Blues Music Awards nominee.\nOver the past 25 
 years Paul has traveled extensively\, performing with Robinson at blues fe
 stivals across the country. Their collaboration continues today and Paul c
 an be heard on Robinson’s latest Delmark release\, Soul in Blue. While t
 ouring with Robinson in 2014\, Paul developed a friendship with Grammy-nom
 inated guitarist Ronnie Earl. The following year Paul released his gospel 
 album In the Hands of God\, which features a guest appearance by Earl. Bet
 ween 2015 and 2018 Paul had the opportunity to perform alongside Ronnie at
  SPACE in Evanston\, Illinois\, as well at the Tampa Bay Blues Fest when E
 arl joined the Tad Robinson band onstage. The recording of In the Hands of
  God sparked a creative partnership with vocalist Rebekah Meldrum. After i
 nviting her to sing on several tracks\, the two began collaborating and we
 nt on to record a live album at the Slippery Noodle and a studio album of 
 original material both of which were released on the legendary Slippery No
 odle label. In addition to his work with all of the aforementioned artists
 \, Paul has contributed to hundreds of recordings by a diverse range of ar
 tists. His work as a guitarist\, songwriter\, producer and collaborator ha
 s made him a respected figure in Indiana’s music community and beyond. F
 ar from slowing down\, Paul continues to pursue new creative opportunities
 . His most recent singles are “The Gift of You “ featuring Tad Robinso
 n on vocals and “The Day that I Met Me”\, a song co written with songw
 riter Jacki Alexander featuring Sarah Scarbrough McLaughlin.\nRebekah Meld
 rum delivers the real thing – raw\, hypnotic\, and drenched in soul. She
  takes audiences on a rich journey through the history of the genre\, from
  swampy Delta roots and backcountry acoustic jams to steamy inner-city gro
 oves and brassy New Orleans rhythms.\nDon’t miss the soul-stirring blues
  experience that will leave you wanting more!
GEO:39.1662844;-86.5328085
LOCATION:Buskirk-Chumley Theater\, 114 E. Kirkwood Avenue\, Bloomington\, 
 IN 47408
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/3rd-annual-bloomington-winter-b
 lues-fest-2027/60212/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
